            <ArticleTitle>Allodynia after acute intrathecal morphine administration in a patient with neuropathic pain after spinal cord injury.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>183-6, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Acute intrathecal administration of relatively small doses of opioids may precipitate neuropathic pain and allodynia in those with spinal cord injury.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
